From b8ce5fc26bc6bd990cec527f73a04abb706f8275 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xs1128 <ooixinsheng@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:29:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Save: copy the state to the host from q_cons_ts(1)

q_cons_ts(2) equals q_cons_ts(1) at a save, but its host copy is never
touched before, so the device-to-host copy of the output first-touched
about 0.5 GB of pages at 201^3. The host copy of q_cons_ts(1) already
holds the initial state. The written values are the same. Unified-memory
builds, which write q_cons_ts(2) from the host, are unchanged.
---
 src/simulation/m_start_up.fpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/simulation/m_start_up.fpp b/src/simulation/m_start_up.fpp
index ed2edff..c3761a8 100644
--- a/src/simulation/m_start_up.fpp
+++ b/src/simulation/m_start_up.fpp
@@ -751,6 +751,11 @@ contains
             $:END_GPU_PARALLEL_LOOP()
             stor = 2
         end if
+#ifndef FRONTIER_UNIFIED
+        ! Copy and write q_cons_ts(1), which q_cons_ts(2) now equals: its host copy already holds the initial state, so the
+        ! device-to-host copies below land in resident pages, while those into q_cons_ts(2) first-touched ~0.5 GB at 201^3.
+        stor = 1
+#endif
 
         call cpu_time(start)
         call nvtxStartRange("SAVE-DATA")
-- 
2.47.3

